ick=\"bcv(26,47,13)\">Ezek 47:13</ref> (<bdbheb>חבלים</bdbheb>; <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Vg')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵑ9</reflink></bdbheb></lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Tg')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵑ7</reflink></bdbheb></lookup> read as dual, see <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Ew')\">Ew</lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Sm')\">Sm</lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Da')\">Da</lookup> and others; <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Co')\">Co</lookup> strike out on internal grounds); of particular regions <bdbheb>אַרְגֹּב</bdbheb> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>ח</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Deut 3:4\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"3\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"3\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(5,3,4)\">Deut 3:4</ref>; <ref ref=\"Deut 3:13\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"3\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"3\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(5,3,13)\">Deut 3:13</ref>; <ref ref=\"Deut 3:14\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"3\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"3\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(5,3,14)\">Deut 3:14</ref>; <ref ref=\"1Kgs 4:13\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"4\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"4\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(11,4,13)\">1Kgs 4:13</ref> <bdbheb>אַכְזִיב</bdbheb> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>ח</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Josh 19:29\" b=\"6\" cBegin=\"19\" vBegin=\"29\" cEnd=\"19\" vEnd=\"29\" onclick=\"bcv(6,19,29)\">Josh 19:29</ref> (si vera 1., see <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('WMM')\">WMM<sup>Asien 194</sup></lookup>); <bdbheb>הַיָּם</bdbheb> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>ח</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Zeph 2:5\" b=\"36\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(36,2,5)\">Zeph 2:5</ref> also v<ref ref=\"Zeph 2:6\" b=\"36\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"6\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"6\" onclick=\"bcv(36,2,6)\">Zeph 2:6</ref>, but <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>היתה ח</bdbheb> here dubious; <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Sta')\">Sta</lookup> proposes 2 feminine singular <bdbheb>הָיִת</bdbheb>, and strike out <bdbheb>הים</bdbheb> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>ח</bdbheb>; without <bdbheb>הים</bdbheb>, v<ref ref=\"Zeph 2:7\" b=\"36\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"7\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"7\" onclick=\"bcv(36,2,7)\">Zeph 2:7</ref>.